# `multigrid::Hierarchy::restrict_to_coarse`

[Back to `multigrid::Hierarchy`](../Hierarchy.md)

Transfers a field from level `l` to the next coarser level `l + 1`.

## Signature

```cpp
[[nodiscard]] pluss::Series multigrid::Hierarchy::restrict_to_coarse(std::size_t l, pluss::Series f) const;
```

## What It Does

The restriction is the adjoint of the linear [prolongation](prolong_from_coarse.md) divided by `2ᵈ`, a weighted average of the fine cells that sit under each coarse cell, with wall-reflected ghosts at the ends. It is the residual transfer of the V-cycle. Level 0 is the finest; `l` must be less than `levels() − 1`.

## Parameters

`std::size_t l`
: The fine level, `0 ≤ l < levels() − 1`.

`pluss::Series f`
: A field on level `l`.

## Returns

The field on level `l + 1`.

## Errors

- A level out of range, or a field of the wrong shape, throws.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Shape and averaging. A constant field on 8 cells restricts to a constant on 4 cells.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace mg = pluss::subsp::math::multigrid;
namespace krylov = pluss::subsp::math::krylov;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const mg::Hierarchy h({.axes = {{8, 1.0, mg::Edge::Periodic, mg::Edge::Periodic}}}, pluss::series::ones({8}, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), [] { mg::Options o; o.coarsest_cells = 2; return o; }());
  out.writeln(h.restrict_to_coarse(0, pluss::series::ones({8}, pluss::ScalarType::Float64)).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2

Two dimensions. A 8×8 field restricts to 4×4.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace mg = pluss::subsp::math::multigrid;
namespace krylov = pluss::subsp::math::krylov;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(0));
  mg::Options o;
  o.coarsest_cells = 4;
  const mg::Hierarchy h({.axes = {{8, 1.0, mg::Edge::Dirichlet, mg::Edge::Dirichlet}, {8, 1.0, mg::Edge::Dirichlet, mg::Edge::Dirichlet}}}, pluss::series::ones({8, 8}, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), o);
  out.writeln("coarse shape =", h.restrict_to_coarse(0, pluss::series::ones({8, 8}, pluss::ScalarType::Float64)).sizes());
}
```

### Example 3

Adjointness. `⟨R f, c⟩ = 2⁻ᵈ ⟨f, P c⟩`: restriction is the transpose of prolongation up to the factor `2ᵈ` (here `d = 1`).

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace mg = pluss::subsp::math::multigrid;
namespace krylov = pluss::subsp::math::krylov;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  mg::Options o;
  o.coarsest_cells = 2;
  const Series f = (pluss::series::arange(0.0, 16.0, 1.0, pluss::ScalarType::Float64) * 0.5).sin();
  const Series c = (pluss::series::arange(0.0, 8.0, 1.0, pluss::ScalarType::Float64) * 0.8).cos();
  const mg::Hierarchy h({.axes = {{16, 1.0, mg::Edge::Dirichlet, mg::Edge::Neumann}}}, f, o);
  out.writeln("<Rf,c> =", (h.restrict_to_coarse(0, f) * c).sum().item<double>(), ", <f,Pc>/2 =", (f * h.prolong_from_coarse(0, c)).sum().item<double>() / 2.0);
}
```

